# Line endings.
#
# This project is Windows-only (see README, "Highlights"), but the
# repository is read and cloned on every platform. Without these rules the
# working tree's line endings depend on each contributor's local
# `core.autocrlf`, and a pull request can arrive showing every line of a
# file as changed when only one line actually was.
#
# The rule is: normalise to LF inside the repository, and let Git decide
# the working-tree ending — except for the three Windows script types that
# must be CRLF on disk to behave correctly when double-clicked or invoked
# by the shell.

* text=auto

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf

*.py   text
*.md   text
*.html text
*.css  text
*.js   text
*.json text
*.yml  text
*.txt  text
*.ini  text

*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
